<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech FinMin T-bill gross yield hits 11.9 pct.</title>
<headline>Czech FinMin T-bill gross yield hits 11.9 pct.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gross yield at the Czech Finance Ministry's auction of a five billion crown tranche of 13-week treasury bills hit 11.9 percent, the Czech National Bank (CNB) said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The CNB added that net yield in the auction was 8.9 percent, and that the auction was heavily oversubscribed with bids totalling 19.894 billion crowns.  </p>
<p>Comparative results were not immediately available.</p>
<p>Dealers said the heavy demand could be attributed in large part to a new 25 percent withholding rate that has in turn forced the ministry to raise yields on its bills.</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 42-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
